{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners feels like a natural next choice because vocal duets connect with the polished ensemble singing and musical standards I have enjoyed.",
    "25 appeals to my interest in expressive singing and melodic ballads; In The Lonely Hour also interests me, though I would choose Partners first."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Noel and Home for Christmas connect with past Christmas listening, but I am not seeking seasonal music in this session.",
    "Elvis: Ultimate Gospel does not connect with an established gospel interest, while Traveller, 21 Number Ones, and The Very Best Of give me too little musical information to judge a match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My previous Christmas selections seem to have been treated as an ongoing desire for seasonal music.",
    "Enjoying strong singers does not mean every vocal collection fits; the songs, arrangements, and style of singing matter to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My ensemble recordings, musical standards, and soundtrack listening suggest that polished voices paired with rich arrangements are a particularly useful connection.",
    "My latest relaxing classical selection suggests a possible interest in gentler listening, and I need a clearer musical connection before choosing unfamiliar titles or compilations."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in expressive vocals but stretched past seasonal listening and broad vocal similarities beyond what I want now."
}"}
